                                          "message":  "Slim the base install: drop loguru, move the Lance stack into a [data] extra (#317)\n\n* remove loguru from deps\n\n* put lance deps in a data extra\n\n* make the OpenCV-backed visual wrappers lazy\n\nWorld needs only MegaWrapper from wrapper.default, which depends on nothing\nbeyond gymnasium/numpy. But wrapper/__init__ also imported .visual eagerly,\nand that module imports cv2 at module scope — so a base install (cv2 ships\nin the [env] extra) lost World to a module it never touches.\n\nResolve the visual names lazily via PEP 562, the same idiom the top-level\nstable_worldmodel/__init__ already uses. MegaWrapper and the other default\nwrappers stay eager; touching a visual wrapper without cv2 now raises an\nImportError naming the extra to install.\n\nNothing in-repo imports a visual wrapper — only MegaWrapper — and there are\nno star-imports of the package, so this is behaviour-preserving wherever cv2\nis present.\n\nBeyond making `import swm.World` work, this unblocks test collection:\ntests/test_world.py, tests/test_new_world.py and tests/test_wrappers.py could\nnot be collected without cv2 (733 -\u003e 873 tests collected; all 140 newly\ncollected tests pass).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
